advisories.ai_summary:
### Summary
The remark42 image proxy fetches an arbitrary remote URL and re-serves the response from remark42's own origin. The download path decides whether the fetched resource is an image by looking only at the `Content-Type` header the remote server claims — it never inspects the actual bytes. An attacker hosts a URL that sets `Content-Type` to `image/png` but returns an HTML/JavaScript body:

* the download check sees `image/png` → accepts it;
* the serve path sniffs the body → emits `Content-Type: text/html`;
* the browser renders attacker HTML/JS as a document in remark42's origin. [CVEs: CVE-2026-48788 | Score: 15.34/100 | Actors: UNC-CDB-INGEST | TTPs: T1105, T1190, T1059]

